# Excel Element Explorer
# This is a debugging/exploration script that helps you discover UI elements
#
# Purpose:
# - Find elements in Excel by intentionally using wrong names
# - See suggestions with similarity scores
# - Understand what elements are available
#
# Prerequisites:
# - Microsoft Excel must be installed
# - Run with debug mode (default) to see suggestions
#
# Usage:
#   ./build/Debug/UniControl examples/example-excel-explorer.unictl
#
# This script will intentionally fail to find elements, showing you:
# - Available buttons in the ribbon
# - Element suggestions with similarity scores
# - What elements can be clicked

# Use continue mode to see ALL errors and suggestions
mode continue

log === Excel Element Explorer ===
log This script will show you available UI elements in Excel

# Launch Excel
log Launching Excel...
launch Excel
wait 3

log
log === Exploring Excel Start Screen ===
log Intentionally searching for non-existent elements to see what's available:

# These will fail but show suggestions
find WorkbookTemplate
find NewDocument
find BlankSheet

log
log === Opening a Blank Workbook ===
# Now find the real one based on suggestions
find Blank Workbook role: AXButton
click
wait 2

log
log === Exploring Excel Ribbon ===
log Searching for non-existent ribbon tabs to see what's available:

# These will fail but show all available ribbon tabs
find HomeTab
find InsertTab
find DeveloperTab
find ViewTab

log
log === Exploring Developer Tab (if available) ===
# Try to find the Developer tab
find Developer role: AXButton
click
wait 1

log
log === Exploring Controls ===
log Searching for non-existent controls to see what's available:

# These will fail but show all available controls
find TextBox
find ButtonControl
find CheckBoxControl

log
log === Explorer Complete ===
log
log Review the debug output above to see:
log 1. Available buttons and their exact names
log 2. Similarity scores for typos and close matches
log 3. Role types (AXButton, AXGroup, etc.)
log
log Use this information to write accurate automation scripts!
